[
  {
    "kind": "fr",
    "id": "FR-RUNTIME-TAPE-002",
    "before": {
      "contentField": "description",
      "content": "Datasette.Tick() enforces MOTOR_DELAY=32,000-cycle ramp (datasette.c:62) before pulse delivery when Tick is timing mechanism. SenseLine=!PlayPressed||!RecordPressed (CIA1  bit 4). TryWritePulse stores pulses in record mode.",
      "status": "closed",
      "acceptanceCriteria": []
    },
    "proposed": {
      "contentField": "description",
      "content": "Datasette transport, tape-sense, motor timing, and recording must reproduce pinned immutable VICE behavior for the same selected machine, tape media state, control sequence, and emulated clock sequence. Machine-specific tape-sense and pulse wiring belong in machine adapters. Internal pulse-buffer success or compatibility with managed-only tests does not establish VICE parity.",
      "status": "pending",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-01",
          "text": "Drive STOP, START, FORWARD, REWIND, and RECORD from a known STOP state with no image, read-only image, and writable image. Each accepted mode and tape-sense transition matches pinned VICE. No-image RECORD and read-only-image RECORD leave mode and sense unchanged; accepted RECORD with writable media asserts sense.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-02",
          "text": "For identical accepted tape-sense transitions, C64 CPU port $0001 input bit 4 and VIC-20 VIA1 port A input bit 6 match pinned VICE, including input/output direction masking. C64 CIA1 FLAG and VIC-20 VIA2 CA1 pulse events are tested separately and are not substituted for tape-sense input.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-03",
          "text": "With an initially stopped motor and no pending datasette alarm, a motor-on transition schedules the startup read alarm at the current emulated clock plus 32000. The ordered read-side event trace immediately before, at, and after that deadline matches pinned VICE. A pre-existing pending alarm is preserved as VICE preserves it; metadata retrieval alone is not counted as a pulse event.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-04",
          "text": "For a running motor, motor-off schedules stopping at current clock plus 32000 without stopping immediately. Motor-on before that stop executes cancels the pending stop without imposing a new startup ramp. Repeated motor-off does not extend an existing stop deadline. Ordered boundary events and restart after an executed stop match pinned VICE.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-05",
          "text": "Recording writes occur only under the native combination of an attached image, accepted RECORD mode, running motor, and qualifying write-line transition. No image, read-only media that rejected RECORD, wrong mode, motor stopped, repeated levels, and nonqualifying transitions produce the same absence of tape writes as pinned VICE.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-06",
          "text": "For identical accepted recording signal traces and media, emitted TAP bytes, elapsed-gap/remainder handling, first-write state, image-position updates, and failure/STOP side effects match pinned VICE. Cover short and long gap boundaries and partial or failed writes; an incremented managed pulse-buffer count alone does not satisfy this criterion.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        }
      ]
    },
    "unchangedFields": [
