    "id": "TR-TAP-EDGE-001",
    "before": {
      "contentField": "description",
      "content": "Datasette.SenseLine = false when PlayPressed or RecordPressed (CIA1  bit 4 active-low). TryWritePulse stores pulse when MotorEnabled && RecordPressed. RecordedPulseCount tracks stored pulses.",
      "status": "closed",
      "acceptanceCriteria": []
    },
    "proposed": {
      "contentField": "description",
      "content": "Model accepted VICE transport state and image eligibility before deriving tape sense or recording eligibility. Preserve the distinction between device sense state, each machine input port, and tape read-pulse interrupt wiring. Recording consumes ordered clocked write-line transitions and retains the native gap, image-position, and write-failure behavior through the managed adapter.",
      "status": "pending",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-01",
          "text": "Use the FR-RUNTIME-TAPE-002 ac-01 media/control matrix to assert accepted mode, sense state, and unchanged state for ignored RECORD commands; do not treat an unconstrained RecordPressed flag as proof that RECORD was accepted.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-02",
          "text": "Use FR-RUNTIME-TAPE-002 ac-02 observations to assert the C64 CPU-port and VIC-20 VIA1 input bits for both data-direction settings; separately assert pulse routing to C64 CIA1 FLAG and VIC-20 VIA2 CA1.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-03",
          "text": "Use the same recording eligibility traces as FR-RUNTIME-TAPE-002 ac-05. Assert emitted writes and absence of writes as well as updated last-write-line state, including input transitions while recording is ineligible.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-04",
          "text": "Use the same recording byte/error traces as FR-RUNTIME-T

