      "contentField": "condition",
      "content": "Validate FR-RUNTIME-TAPE-002 ac-01/ac-02/ac-05/ac-06 and every TR-TAP-EDGE-001 criterion with shared media, accepted transport-command, machine-port, and write-line fixtures. Establish correct and discriminating incorrect mocks before product changes, then reuse the same cases and assertions against managed and immutable native providers. Historical seven-test success is not an acceptance condition.",
      "status": "pending",
      "acceptanceCriteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-01",
          "text": "TransportSense_MediaCommandMatrix covers the five transport commands from STOP for absent/read-only/writable media and subsequent STOP transitions. Correct mocks assert accepted mode and sense; wrong polarity, ignored-command state changes, and omitted transitions are rejected.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-02",
          "text": "MachineSense_C64CpuPortAndVic20Via1 covers both machines and input/output masking. TapeRead_PulseInterruptRouting separately verifies CIA1 FLAG and VIA2 CA1. Wrong port, bit, DDR handling, interrupt target, and extra interrupts are rejected by negative controls.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-03",
          "text": "Recording_EligibilityAndWriteEdges covers attached versus absent media, RECORD accepted versus rejected, running versus stopped motor, and qualifying versus repeated/opposite write levels. Correct mocks assert writes and no-writes plus state changes; the historical no-tape successful-write behavior must be rejected.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-04",
          "text": "Recording_GapEncodingAndFailures covers elapsed gaps 0,6,7,8,2046,2047, short-gap remainder carry, first-write state, TAP v0/v1/v2 paths supported by the pinned source, and first/partial/failed output writes. Assert emitted bytes, image position, dirty state and STOP side effects against independently pinned expectations.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-05",
          "text": "Real-provider validation reuses all fixtures and assertions with actual immutable VICE and managed observations, followed by the full cumulative native-safe and real-emulator gates. Preserve historical tests/evidence, explicitly record superseded wrong expectations, and require zero failed, skipped or aborted cases plus accepted hostile validation before satisfaction.",
          "isSatisfied": false
        }
      ],
      "title": "Datasette transport, sense wiring and recording parity"
